/// A closure an initializer makes captures a bare local declared after it,
/// and reads the value the first statement assigns (newspeak-spec.pdf 3.6).
/// The editor hints' behaviour oracle (`ns-analyzer`'s `hinted_goldens`)
/// depends on this golden: "apply all" moves the assignment into
/// `count`'s declaration, and must then leave `count` mutable, as a
/// read-only `count` would let the optimized lowering copy its nil into
/// the closure.
class BareLocalCapturedBeforeItsAssignment = Object new () (
  public main: platform args: arguments = (
    |
      transcript = platform transcript.
      reader = [count].
      count
    |
    count:: 1.
    transcript
        show: reader value printString;
        newLine.
  )
)
